        <item>
            <title>2.38.0</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 13:41:36 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>124</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.38.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Features
- **Other Macs' sessions in the sidebar.** Every Mac publishing to the same relay now gets its own section, listing its open Claude Code sessions with the same activity dots as local ones. Click a row to attach to that session in a pane — tmux-attach style, over the Mac's live mirror — and type into it as if it were local. A Mac that stops publishing is dimmed after five minutes; a session that is not running on its Mac is greyed out with a tooltip saying so.
- **Pair two Macs.** Settings › Mobile › Other Macs: paste the connection string another Mac copies from its own Settings ("Copy Connection"), and its sessions become attachable. The password stays in the Keychain. The button and toggle are now named for any device, not only the iPhone.
- **Remote directory browser: New Folder and hidden files.** The SSH browser's bottom bar has New Folder… (Enter creates, Esc cancels) and a Show hidden checkbox, off by default and remembered across sheets.

### Changes
- The roster sent to the phone now carries every open session, not only the ones in a pane, each with a `live` flag. The iPhone app 1.x reads it and opens a session that is not running offline instead of attempting an attach. Older phone builds keep working and simply see more rows.
- A mirror pane that loses its connection shows "Connection to <Mac> Lost" with Retry; a refused or unreachable attach closes the pane and says why in both the launcher and the sidebar.
- Attaching to a long or image-heavy session replays as much of the transcript as fits the connection, newest turns first.
]]></description>
